<newsitem itemid="30692" id="root" date="1996-09-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>AUSTRALIA: Nat Foods 95/96 net up, dividend cut.</title>
<headline>Nat Foods 95/96 net up, dividend cut.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    37.56 vs 37.02</p>
<p>    Net				     15.05 vs 10.77</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		2.5 vs 3.00</p>
<p>NOTE: National Foods Ltd is a dairy and fruit juice group.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		5.5 vs 6.5</p>
<p>    Abnormals			 loss 7.89 vs loss 8.40</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			1.15 vs 1.06</p>
<p>    Other income			  17.48 vs  18.58</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     8.7 vs 7.6</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date Nov 1</p>
<p>Reg date Oct 25</p>
<p>    Tax				     14.87 vs 12.92</p>
<p>    Interest				15.57 vs 12.27</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  22.78 vs 17.13</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.06 vs 0.21</p>
<p>NOTE: National Foods said the abnormal loss mainly reflected corporate restructuring costs, loss on property joint venture, loss on sale of investment in Mildura Fruit Juices Australia Pty Ltd and write-off on Yoplait establishment costs.</p>
<p>NOTE: Earnings before abnormals, interest and tax by industry:</p>
<p>    Market milk and diary foods     35.24 vs 32.12</p>
<p>    Fruit beverages/processed fruit  3.36 vs  2.07</p>
<p>    Consumer products		   18.59 vs 14.45</p>
<p>    Unallocated		     loss 4.05 vs loss 4.36</p>
<p>NOTE: Earnings before abnormals, interest and tax by geographical segment:</p>
<p>    Australia			     49.23 vs 41.42</p>
<p>    New Zealand			    5.77 vs  5.19</p>
<p>    Other			     loss 1.88 vs loss 2.32</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
